# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository AND on checkout, on every
# platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with `core.autocrlf=true` gets CRLF on disk while
# Prettier's `endOfLine` default expects LF. The result is that
# `npm run format:check` fails locally on files nobody has touched — and passes
# in CI on Linux — so `prepublishOnly` is red on a developer machine and green on
# the build server. `eol=lf` overrides `core.autocrlf`, so this holds regardless
# of each contributor's git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be normalised — line-ending translation corrupts them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.pdf binary
*.tgz binary
